  "id": "substance-abuse-treatment",
  "term": "substance abuse treatment",
  "definition": "Substance abuse treatment is care aimed at helping people with problematic substance use reduce or stop harmful use. In the source, it is described as a treatment area that has often emphasized compliance and stopping the behavior, while newer approaches also use psychotherapeutic methods and the therapeutic relationship to reduce resistance and support client autonomy.",
